    "room_rects": "Rooms tile the gross footprint without overlap. floor_rects are zoning rectangles, not clear wall-to-wall measurements.",
    "walls": "a/b are wall centerlines. at is metres from a along a→b. Remove openings from the actual mesh between bottom/top; do not cover with a panel.",
    "sliding_doors": "clear_intervals use distance from wall.a; fixed/parked glazed leaves must not occupy those intervals.",
    "hinged_doors": "open_leaf explicitly gives hinge and open tip in XY; keep their swept footprint free.",
    "beds": "Bed size is unrotated local [width,length,height]; head points local +Y at rotation 0. rotation_z_degrees rotates model and footprint.",
    "windows": "All four bedroom heads and full-height wardrobes are on internal or opaque wall segments; low desks may sit below 0.85m sills.",
    "integration": "Standalone Blender prototype only; no existing campus geometry, units, storeys or metadata are changed.",
    "furniture": "Furniture footprints are planning reservations, not assertions of final mesh bounds. When collision_rects exist, use those solid parts for planning navigation; decorative rugs are walkable.",
